# Normalize all text files to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# The independent-review source manifest (scripts/file_policy.py: source_manifest)
# hashes raw file bytes, so a CRLF checkout on Windows and an LF checkout on Linux
# produce different hashes for the same committed blob — which makes review_gate
# report review-stale on one platform but not the other. Pinning eol=lf keeps the
# working tree byte-identical across the ubuntu-latest and windows-latest CI jobs
# so the committed review manifest matches on both. text=auto still lets git
# auto-detect and leave binary files untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
